  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 307 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\n...Synopsis...\n\nNorthwest flow prevails aloft this afternoon into the overnight \nhours ahead of a weak H5 shortwave. Upper flow briefly becomes \nwesterly as the trough moves across the area late Tuesday into early \nWednesday. A low chance for light rain will accompany the trough, \nwith the best chances for measurable precipitation remaining \nprimarily south of Highway 2. The probability for 0.1 inch of rain \nis holding steady at about 30 percent in west central Minnesota, \nwith lower chances elsewhere. \n\nMuch cooler air filters into the Northern Plains and Upper Midwest \nas the trough slides eastward and northerly H5 flow develops. \nToday's high temperatures will reach the upper 50s to near 60 \ndegrees; however, temps begin a downward trend heading into Tuesday \nas cloud cover overspreads the area and light rain moves across the \nsouthern half of the forecast area. Highs on Tuesday are expected to \nreach the upper 40s to low 50s. Temps fall to near normal heading \ninto the Wednesday through Friday period, with highs in the upper \n30s to near 40 degrees, and overnight lows in the 20s.",
